  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pilot Access to Finance &#x2013; Digitalisation Guarantee Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Entrepreneurship is an important mechanism to realise increases in aggregate well-being. For entrepreneurship to flourish, young entrepreneurs need to be able to start their companies and attract the right capital to grow their company. However, access to financing opportunities are lacking in the Democratic Republice of the Congo (DRC). The government released the Fonds de Garantie de l&#x2019;Entrepreneuriat au Congo (FOGEC), which is supposed to provide aspiring loan takers with the necessary guarantee that, if they cannot pay back their loans, FOGEC will step in. This will increase their chances of obtaining a loan from a bank in DRC. The process of applying for FOGEC is at this point not very accessible, especially for people in rural areas. By digitalising this process, FOGEC can support more aspiring loan takers, and more entrepreneurs will get the possibility to get a loan from a bank. This will in turn result in business growth, economic growth and improvement of the employment rate.</narrative>
  </description>
